      Historical minutes show that when the committee cannot agree on the Chair’s proposal it
typically negotiates a mid-point compromise rather than mechanically retaining the prior setting
(e.g. the August 1989 and June 2003 meetings). This median fallback matches that practice and
avoids artificially inflating policy inertia.




